Rich-Harris/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rich-Harris/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rich-Harris/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-04-22T13:13:41Z","updated_at":"2021-04-22T13:13:41Z","body":"Ah, whoops 😬  This is happening because there's error handling here... https://github.com/sveltejs/kit/blob/9883c179720aeff37c9d6db4b5b37ed9e61e3c7c/packages/kit/src/core/dev/index.js#L139-L141 ...so that you can get away with not having a `hooks.js` file.\r\n\r\nSince that (terrible) code was written, we added a `resolve_entry` helper here... https://github.com/sveltejs/kit/blob/9883c179720aeff37c9d6db4b5b37ed9e61e3c7c/packages/kit/src/core/utils.js#L44-L71 ...which would allow us to check if the file exists before attempting to load it, which would make the error 'handling' unnecessary. Should be a quick win if anyone wants to rustle up a PR (the only finicky part would be adding a test since we'd have to add a whole new 'app' to `packages/kit/test/apps` with a failing `hooks.js`; I think we can get away without adding one).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sveltejs/kit/issues/comments/824830490/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"Rich-Harris","id":1162160,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjIxNjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1162160?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rich-Harris","html_url":"https://github.com/Rich-Harris","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rich-Harris/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rich-Harris/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rich-Harris/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rich-Harris/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_